    }), "\n", _jsx(_components.p, {
      children: "The Dependency Inversion Principle states that high-level modules should not depend on low-level modules; both should depend on abstractions. In prompt engineering, this means your orchestration logic shouldn't depend on specific LLM providers, models, or prompting strategies. A high-level process like \"generate research report\" should depend on abstractions like \"retrieves relevant documents\" and \"synthesizes information,\" not on \"calls GPT-4 with specific prompt template X using OpenAI API.\""
